			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Standardize formatting, upgrade dependencies, and introduce Spine action client\n\nThis commit applies `rustfmt` standards across the Grove codebase, upgrades core dependencies, and introduces a dedicated client for Spine/EchoAction protocols.\n\n**Code Formatting & Renaming:**\n- Applied consistent formatting (K&R braces, reduced vertical spacing) across all modules.\n- Renamed `GrpcTransport` and `IpctTransport` to `gRPCTransport` and `IPCTransport` to adhere to naming conventions (acronyms in PascalCase).\n- Standardized method visibility and casing in `SpineConnection` (e.g., `Connect` vs `connect`).\n\n**Dependency Updates:**\n- Upgraded `wasmtime` from `19.0` to `20.0`.\n- Removed `wasmtime-wasi` and `wasi-common` as dependencies.\n- Made `tonic` and `prost` optional features to support builds without gRPC.\n- Added `semver` and `chrono` for protocol and time handling.\n\n**New Features:**\n- **SpineActionClient:** Added `Source/Protocol/SpineActionClient.rs`, a new gRPC client for handling `EchoAction` communication with the Mountain backend. This provides a structured interface for bidirectional actions, host registration, and heartbeat management.\n- **SpineConnection Refactor:** Refactored `SpineConnection` to utilize the new client structure, introducing `HeartbeatConfig`, `ConnectionMetrics`, and simplified state management.\n\n**Impact:** Improves code maintainability and consistency while laying the groundwork for robust, typed communication with the Mountain backend.",
			"SHA": "07643474e5a54440238b4865acd7ebddbca2f543"
		},
